WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:06.161
Niccolò Machiavelli.

00:00:07.436 --> 00:00:11.125
Probably one of the most
highly acclaimed philosophers

00:00:11.357 --> 00:00:13.270
and political theorists
of all time.

00:00:13.975 --> 00:00:16.666
Also, one of my
greatest influences

00:00:16.896 --> 00:00:21.944
and a figure that has been referenced,
quoted, and misunderstood like few.

00:00:23.046 --> 00:00:27.469
But before I initiate my attempt to
scrutinize Machiavelli and his philosophy,

00:00:27.818 --> 00:00:29.370
I want to ask you a question.

00:00:30.119 --> 00:00:32.579
When somebody mentions
the name Machiavelli,

00:00:32.649 --> 00:00:36.056
or the terms Machiavellian
and Machiavellianism,

00:00:36.699 --> 00:00:38.842
what is the first thing
that comes to your mind?

00:00:39.523 --> 00:00:44.762
I assume that you think of words like
dark triad, duplicity, and manipulation.

00:00:45.769 --> 00:00:49.548
Or in a broader context
the ability to gain power

00:00:49.928 --> 00:00:53.170
through deception, insincerity,
and abuse of power.

00:00:53.959 --> 00:00:55.868
Actually, those are all wrong.

00:00:56.749 --> 00:01:01.028
They do play a role in the way Machiavelli
expressed his political theories,

00:01:01.053 --> 00:01:04.563
but they all fail to paint an
accurate picture of the man.

00:01:05.523 --> 00:01:09.738
If there is a word that could accurately
describe Machiavelli and his ideas,

00:01:09.992 --> 00:01:12.294
it is this: Pragmatism.

00:01:13.357 --> 00:01:15.984
He was probably the first
political theorist

00:01:16.349 --> 00:01:18.563
that escaped the
delusion of idealism

00:01:18.936 --> 00:01:23.873
and honestly proposed pragmatic solutions
and interpretations of government.

00:01:24.832 --> 00:01:29.278
Apparently, his views were dramatically
influenced by the time he lived in

00:01:30.273 --> 00:01:31.627
and his personal experiences,

00:01:31.968 --> 00:01:35.523
oftentimes exceeding the threshold
of political correctness

00:01:35.912 --> 00:01:39.653
and blurring the lines between
morally right and morally wrong.

00:01:40.348 --> 00:01:44.944
Nonetheless, they constitute a
powerful compendium of knowledge

00:01:45.265 --> 00:01:50.189
that is shaping the interpretation of
power and influence till this very day.

00:01:53.639 --> 00:01:57.037
Niccolo di Bernardo
dei Machiavelli

00:01:57.572 --> 00:02:01.500
was born in 1469 in
Florence, Italy.

00:02:02.285 --> 00:02:06.617
His family was descended from
the old rulers of Tuscany

00:02:07.148 --> 00:02:09.186
and they have
produced many members

00:02:09.211 --> 00:02:11.547
that were part of the
government of the time.

00:02:12.430 --> 00:02:16.161
Back then, Italy consisted
of many city-states

00:02:16.186 --> 00:02:18.839
that were usually ruled
by different Houses.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:22.991
Florence was among the largest
city-states in Europe

00:02:23.517 --> 00:02:27.289
and was considered one of the
wealthiest and most successful.

00:02:28.394 --> 00:02:32.030
Part of this success should be
attributed to the “House of Medici”

00:02:32.594 --> 00:02:35.173
which was one of the strongest
families of the time.

00:02:35.944 --> 00:02:38.591
The Medici controlled
the Medici bank

00:02:38.798 --> 00:02:41.214
– then Europe’s largest bank –

00:02:41.641 --> 00:02:45.849
and this allowed them to expand their
influence and strategic alliances.

00:02:47.127 --> 00:02:50.967
In 1494, after a popular revolt,

00:02:51.174 --> 00:02:56.341
the Medici were expulsed from power and
Florence was restored to a republic.

00:02:57.158 --> 00:03:01.193
It was then that Machiavelli
received his first government role

00:03:01.218 --> 00:03:03.802
as the person responsible
for the production

00:03:04.158 --> 00:03:07.325
of official Florentine
government documents.

00:03:07.995 --> 00:03:12.493
Machiavelli was part of a government
that wanted to liberate Florence

00:03:12.524 --> 00:03:16.207
from the Medici reign, but
that was far from easy.

00:03:16.714 --> 00:03:19.790
The Medici had a strong
alliance with the Pope

00:03:20.174 --> 00:03:23.487
and their recapture of
Florence was a matter of time.

00:03:24.323 --> 00:03:29.706
Machiavelli’s career was quite
turbulent and ended sadly in 1512

00:03:30.087 --> 00:03:34.809
when he was deprived of office after
the Medici won a critical battle

00:03:35.039 --> 00:03:38.048
that helped them emerge
to power once again.

00:03:39.095 --> 00:03:44.071
In 1513, the Medici accused Machiavelli
of conspiracy against them

00:03:44.476 --> 00:03:47.008
and had him imprisoned
and tortured.

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:50.345
After denying involvement,
he was released

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:55.762
and decided to retire to his estate
at Sant’Andrea in Percussina

00:03:56.134 --> 00:03:59.333
in order to devote himself
to studying and writing.

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:04.708
That’s when he completed his seminal
works “The Prince” and “Discourses”

00:04:05.048 --> 00:04:07.094
and that’s when he
gained his reputation

00:04:07.119 --> 00:04:10.024
as a great political
theorist and philosopher.

00:04:17.063 --> 00:04:21.859
When Machiavelli turned to the
question of whether it was better

00:04:22.336 --> 00:04:25.119
for a prince to be loved or feared

00:04:25.698 --> 00:04:30.273
he stated that while it would be
wonderful for a leader to be both,

00:04:30.722 --> 00:04:32.920
he should eventually
side with fear.

00:04:33.897 --> 00:04:37.780
Machiavelli suggests that human
nature is somewhat ungrateful,

00:04:38.103 --> 00:04:39.911
fickle and dissembling.

00:04:40.468 --> 00:04:43.031
The prince (or any
person in power)

00:04:43.643 --> 00:04:47.706
is like the authority figure that
substitutes the parent figure

00:04:48.143 --> 00:04:50.151
when a person enters adulthood.

00:04:51.269 --> 00:04:55.931
People in power will always have a huge
responsibility towards their followers.

00:04:56.579 --> 00:04:59.407
This responsibility creates
a form of dependency

00:04:59.432 --> 00:05:02.633
that urges people to
keep craving more

00:05:02.865 --> 00:05:07.448
and hold the prince accountable
for most of their needs.

00:05:08.476 --> 00:05:10.282
Such an intense interplay

00:05:10.307 --> 00:05:14.068
damages most of the ability
to cultivate self-reliance

00:05:14.472 --> 00:05:18.013
and people, instead of appreciating
the prince’s offerings,

00:05:18.436 --> 00:05:22.947
they become ungrateful and
keep asking for more.

00:05:23.937 --> 00:05:27.278
Therefore, a prince needs
to resemble characteristics

00:05:27.303 --> 00:05:30.104
that don’t allow others to
question his authority.

00:05:31.111 --> 00:05:33.085
Such a characteristic is fear.

00:05:33.532 --> 00:05:37.019
Fear, although it still
creates a dependency

00:05:37.044 --> 00:05:38.979
between the ruler
and the people,

00:05:39.436 --> 00:05:42.405
it successfully prevents
unwanted behaviors

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:44.508
stemming from lack
of appreciation.

00:05:45.777 --> 00:05:50.102
The trick here is to ensure that
fear doesn’t turn into hatred.

00:05:50.738 --> 00:05:54.906
Intense, cruel and unjustified
demonstrations of fear

00:05:54.952 --> 00:05:56.850
can never keep people engaged.

00:05:57.542 --> 00:06:02.775
Fear needs to be subtly induced in
a way that people can justify it.

00:06:03.309 --> 00:06:07.175
Events of punishment should be
subject to convincing reasoning,

00:06:07.507 --> 00:06:11.743
for people will side with the
most persuasive argument.

00:06:15.643 --> 00:06:19.896
In Chapter 15 of “The Prince,”
Machiavelli states the following:

00:06:20.548 --> 00:06:25.562
“Men have imagined republics
and principalities

00:06:25.607 --> 00:06:28.266
that never really
existed at all.

00:06:28.722 --> 00:06:34.731
Yet the way men live is so far removed
from the way they ought to live

00:06:35.253 --> 00:06:39.606
that anyone who abandons
what is for what should be

00:06:40.166 --> 00:06:43.952
pursues his downfall rather
than his preservation;

00:06:44.325 --> 00:06:48.143
for a man who strives
after goodness

00:06:48.429 --> 00:06:51.737
in all his acts is
sure to come to ruin,

00:06:51.980 --> 00:06:55.230
since there are so many
men who are not good.”

00:06:56.818 --> 00:07:02.089
In this passage, Machiavelli exudes
the totality of his pragmatic ideals.

00:07:02.753 --> 00:07:05.255
He exposes the reality
of human nature

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:09.607
and explains that being constantly
nice will get you nowhere

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:12.402
because most people
are not that nice.

00:07:13.056 --> 00:07:15.771
In short, he tries to explain that

00:07:16.029 --> 00:07:21.358
a prince should destroy the delusion
that acting good will always favor him,

00:07:21.683 --> 00:07:26.172
but at the same time create the
illusion that he is actually good,

00:07:26.563 --> 00:07:28.849
for people respect goodness.

00:07:31.928 --> 00:07:34.550
In general, some
personal characteristics

00:07:34.575 --> 00:07:38.195
will earn people praise,
others condemnation.

00:07:39.016 --> 00:07:44.125
Courage, compassion, faith,
craftiness, and generosity

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:47.269
number among the qualities
that receive praise.

00:07:48.015 --> 00:07:52.658
Cowardice, cruelty,
stubbornness, and miserliness

00:07:53.087 --> 00:07:55.096
are usually met
with condemnation.

00:07:55.793 --> 00:08:01.108
Ideally, a prince would possess all the
qualities deemed “good” by others.

00:08:01.722 --> 00:08:04.389
But this expectation is unrealistic.

00:08:05.205 --> 00:08:08.150
A prince’s first job is
to safeguard the state,

00:08:08.467 --> 00:08:14.385
and alas, harboring “bad” characteristics
is sometimes necessary for this end.

00:08:18.889 --> 00:08:23.462
The relationship between the prince and
the people is quite a turbulent one.

00:08:24.269 --> 00:08:26.936
People demand actions,
but at the same time,

00:08:27.222 --> 00:08:30.832
they are not ready to react
maturely to difficult situations.

00:08:31.579 --> 00:08:35.719
In order to understand the impact
this dynamic has in the relationship,

00:08:35.770 --> 00:08:37.585
we need to work with an analogy.

00:08:38.292 --> 00:08:41.221
Think of a difficult romantic
relationship you had.

00:08:41.793 --> 00:08:44.901
After the honeymoon face,
reality hits you hard

00:08:44.926 --> 00:08:49.056
and most times one of the parties
will let their mask of sanity slip.

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:53.601
False expectations, neurotic
reactions, unmet needs,

00:08:53.626 --> 00:08:56.662
and increased familiarity
will lead to friction

00:08:56.709 --> 00:08:59.852
and an inability to maintain
a stable connection.

00:09:00.754 --> 00:09:04.342
Despite your most courageous
attempts to be honest,

00:09:04.872 --> 00:09:09.150
your partner keeps reacting negatively
to news that don’t suit their liking.

00:09:09.762 --> 00:09:13.575
Your ability to communicate
honest views decreases with time

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:18.653
and inevitably you become dishonest
in order to avoid conflict.

00:09:19.658 --> 00:09:23.702
In a romantic relationship, usually
you have the luxury to leave,

00:09:24.198 --> 00:09:27.302
but a prince doesn’t wish
to abandon his position.

00:09:27.873 --> 00:09:30.421
He decides to embrace dishonesty

00:09:30.801 --> 00:09:34.865
as the most effective weapon
to deal with lack of conflict.

00:09:35.713 --> 00:09:40.588
People will almost always favor a
delusional hope to a harsh truth.

00:09:48.659 --> 00:09:51.346
In Chapters 6-9 of “The Prince,”

00:09:51.413 --> 00:09:54.487
Machiavelli explains what
a prince needs to do

00:09:54.929 --> 00:09:58.828
after he acquires his position depending
on the way he ascended to power.

00:09:59.611 --> 00:10:02.128
The overarching theme
of this idea is that

00:10:02.437 --> 00:10:04.717
loyalty needs to be
constantly scrutinized

00:10:04.987 --> 00:10:07.648
and bought and resistance
to be crushed.

00:10:08.516 --> 00:10:12.270
When it comes to loyalty, the people
who decide to be on the prince’s side

00:10:12.468 --> 00:10:17.414
will do so because they can benefit
from him and not because they like him.

00:10:18.152 --> 00:10:19.518
They are bound to the prince

00:10:19.543 --> 00:10:22.778
and their loyalty is a matter
of character and benefits.

00:10:23.515 --> 00:10:24.765
The prince needs to ensure

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:28.552
that the rapacious and overly
ambitious shouldn’t be trusted

00:10:29.016 --> 00:10:30.897
and that the weak-spirited
and grateful

00:10:30.922 --> 00:10:33.302
should be sought after
and constantly praised.

00:10:33.929 --> 00:10:37.005
That is a subtle but great
detail to identify.

00:10:37.521 --> 00:10:40.510
Overly ambitious people
can’t stay loyal for long.

00:10:40.944 --> 00:10:42.673
They are also thirsty for power

00:10:43.086 --> 00:10:46.016
and eventually will try and
sabotage those above them.

00:10:46.786 --> 00:10:48.735
In contrast, people
who are weak-spirited

00:10:48.760 --> 00:10:51.275
will always savor their
relationship with a prince

00:10:51.624 --> 00:10:55.368
because it allows them to feel safe
and that they belong to his tribe.

00:10:56.460 --> 00:10:59.823
When it comes to resistance
Machiavelli recognizes resistance

00:10:59.848 --> 00:11:01.404
as an omnipresent force.

00:11:02.103 --> 00:11:05.582
That is because people are naturally
resistant to change and reform.

00:11:05.691 --> 00:11:10.245
Especially people who benefited from
the old order will resist fiercely.

00:11:11.285 --> 00:11:13.570
Princes who keep the
old order around

00:11:13.595 --> 00:11:15.849
will inevitably need
to keep fighting them

00:11:16.143 --> 00:11:19.995
and that suggests a waste of
time, resources, and trust.

00:11:20.587 --> 00:11:22.609
Ergo, people who resist,

00:11:22.992 --> 00:11:25.362
need to be crushed
on a whim and fast

00:11:25.387 --> 00:11:28.957
so that the prince can focus
on reassuring the followers

00:11:29.214 --> 00:11:32.951
of the strength of the new order
and the benefits that will follow.

00:11:37.754 --> 00:11:42.024
In Chapter 25, Machiavelli
tries to conclude his ideas

00:11:42.365 --> 00:11:46.452
with the main strategy to be followed
by countries and individuals

00:11:46.754 --> 00:11:48.927
in order to increase their
chances of success.

00:11:49.722 --> 00:11:55.217
Free will vs determinism has always
been a hot topic among thinkers.

00:11:55.781 --> 00:11:59.421
Machiavelli’s stance on the
matter is again very pragmatic.

00:12:00.158 --> 00:12:04.102
According to him, success is the point
where preparation meets opportunity.

00:12:04.978 --> 00:12:06.867
A person cannot control the world,

00:12:06.892 --> 00:12:10.060
but he can definitely control
most of his actions.

00:12:10.817 --> 00:12:11.913
Through foresight,

00:12:11.938 --> 00:12:16.603
people can shield themselves against
misfortune and self-sabotage.

00:12:17.667 --> 00:12:20.173
Moreover, because time changes,

00:12:20.404 --> 00:12:25.372
a prince needs to adapt and embrace
malleable characteristics.

00:12:26.007 --> 00:12:29.931
On the whole, impetuosity
surpasses caution

00:12:30.261 --> 00:12:34.468
and fortune favors energetic
youth over cautious age.

00:12:36.008 --> 00:12:39.678
Machiavellian tactics and
strategies might come across

00:12:39.703 --> 00:12:42.702
as quite caustic and
even dangerous for some.

00:12:43.532 --> 00:12:47.603
For me, his works are invariably
imbued with a sense of awe

00:12:48.119 --> 00:12:51.349
and they constitute a
combustible body of knowledge.

00:12:52.007 --> 00:12:53.838
Actually, “The
Prince” is suggested

00:12:53.863 --> 00:12:57.983
in most political science programs
around the world as a must-read.

00:12:58.714 --> 00:13:00.145
This is not by accident.

00:13:00.658 --> 00:13:03.354
Those principles have
been espoused and applied

00:13:03.379 --> 00:13:07.987
by the most successful political
figures of our past and our present.

00:13:08.667 --> 00:13:12.791
Knowing and understanding
those principles

00:13:13.223 --> 00:13:17.977
can be a crucial step forwards in
redressing the balance within ourselves

00:13:18.388 --> 00:13:21.498
and eventually within
our political system.

00:13:23.944 --> 00:13:24.958
Hi everyone,

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:28.570
Today’s video was something I was
really looking forward to creating.

00:13:29.261 --> 00:13:32.054
And that’s not only because
Machiavelli is one of the thinkers

00:13:32.079 --> 00:13:33.864
that have influenced
my worldview,

00:13:34.237 --> 00:13:38.224
but also because I wanted to shed
some light on some misconceptions

00:13:38.249 --> 00:13:41.601
that tend to be associated
with him and his philosophy.

00:13:42.318 --> 00:13:44.454
Additionally, in our current epoch

00:13:44.479 --> 00:13:48.958
where politics are not considered
anymore this elusive concept

00:13:49.015 --> 00:13:52.379
that seems so far-fetched
and abstract,

00:13:52.714 --> 00:13:55.275
but more like a skill
with certain mechanics

00:13:55.300 --> 00:13:57.744
that can be construed
and cultivated,

00:13:58.143 --> 00:14:00.438
it is our duty to look
into its mechanics

00:14:00.463 --> 00:14:03.452
in order to understand the extent
to which we can influence it

00:14:03.857 --> 00:14:07.276
and as a result improve and
evolve our political system.

